WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.100 --> 00:03.170
The person I have a crush on is you, Suzuki.

3
00:03.170 --> 00:06.300
You really...

4
00:06.300 --> 00:07.940
like me?

5
00:07.940 --> 00:13.270
Then let's keep going, until it's hammered into your head.

6
00:20.000 --> 00:21.720
A dream?

7
00:23.200 --> 00:27.280
[Haruto Serizawa: You were as cute as ever] [Love you - Night]

8
00:28.120 --> 00:31.000
Phew...

9
00:31.000 --> 00:33.490
It wasn't a dream.

10
00:37.880 --> 00:42.390
It's been one week since Serizawa and I started going out.

11
00:46.000 --> 00:49.810
Honestly, I still can't believe it.

12
00:53.420 --> 00:55.400
Morning, Suzuki.

13
00:55.400 --> 00:57.130
Morning.

14
00:58.980 --> 01:00.960
You're looking as cute as ever.

15
01:09.030 --> 01:10.810
Love you.

16
01:15.590 --> 01:18.300
We're being assertive bright and early today.

17
01:18.300 --> 01:19.700
No, it's just,

18
01:19.700 --> 01:24.040
I wanted to make sure I wasn't dreaming.

19
01:24.040 --> 01:25.920
What?

20
01:25.920 --> 01:29.100
Get used to it already.

21
01:29.100 --> 01:32.400
But you're "the" Serizawa.

22
01:34.050 --> 01:37.680
You can check if I'm real all you want.

23
01:37.680 --> 01:40.300
But later, when we're alone, okay?

24
01:44.620 --> 01:47.910
Aw, you're so cute when you're embarrassed.

25
01:48.840 --> 01:52.360
Seriously, how much more time do you need

26
01:52.360 --> 01:55.390
to accept the reality that is me?

27
02:00.490 --> 02:02.450
Come on, let's go.

28
02:11.420 --> 02:15.740
He makes a fair point.

29
02:15.740 --> 02:19.440
Especially given the fact

30
02:19.440 --> 02:22.430
that we've already kissed four times now.

31
02:25.530 --> 02:30.800
Our first kiss was before we confessed.

32
02:30.800 --> 02:34.640
Our second, to commemorate our relationship.

33
02:34.640 --> 02:37.060
Our third, was three days ago.

34
02:37.060 --> 02:39.070
Serizawa!

35
02:39.070 --> 02:41.010
Wait, I can't breathe...

36
02:41.010 --> 02:43.640
Breathe in from your nose.

37
02:43.640 --> 02:45.670
Our fourth kiss

38
02:46.880 --> 02:49.290
was yesterday, after school.

39
02:52.180 --> 02:54.210
And now...

40
02:54.210 --> 02:56.270
Where are we going?

41
02:56.270 --> 02:59.060
Just follow me.

42
03:09.460 --> 03:11.520
Our fifth.

43
03:14.010 --> 03:15.630
See?

44
03:15.630 --> 03:17.820
Not a dream.

45
03:20.010 --> 03:21.530
Yeah.

46
03:24.580 --> 03:29.320
I know this is really happening.

47
03:29.320 --> 03:31.790
I understand that.

48
03:31.790 --> 03:33.780
Still...

49
04:17.900 --> 04:18.930
[Banana Lake]

50
04:18.930 --> 04:22.330
How is that a problem? [Episode 11]

51
04:22.330 --> 04:24.120
Like I already said...

52
04:24.120 --> 04:26.400
Iwasaki, are you even listening?

53
04:26.400 --> 04:27.900
Nope, sorry.

54
04:27.900 --> 04:29.520
What's the issue?

55
04:29.520 --> 04:33.000
According to Suzuki, his Serizawa is, quote:

56
04:33.000 --> 04:34.920
"Too cool".

57
04:34.920 --> 04:36.380
What?

58
04:36.380 --> 04:37.820
To be exact,

59
04:37.820 --> 04:40.800
my Serizawa is too cool for his own good.

60
04:40.800 --> 04:43.200
Same thing.

61
04:43.200 --> 04:44.860
At this point, you're bragging.

62
04:44.860 --> 04:46.660
I am not!

63
04:46.660 --> 04:49.350
This is a real problem for me.

64
04:49.350 --> 04:53.000
Serizawa always makes me so flustered.

65
04:53.000 --> 04:55.040
As if that weren't bad enough,

66
04:55.040 --> 04:59.550
I can't even breathe through my nose when we kiss!

67
04:59.550 --> 05:02.160
Serizawa's always composed,

68
05:02.160 --> 05:03.780
but I easily freak out,

69
05:03.780 --> 05:06.640
and tend to worry alone.

70
05:06.640 --> 05:09.360
The fact that my first boyfriend is so cool

71
05:09.360 --> 05:14.240
makes me think the very world is being thrown off balance.

72
05:19.410 --> 05:23.320
Why are you all grinning?

73
05:23.320 --> 05:25.140
You're adorable.

74
05:25.140 --> 05:26.880
Did any of you get all that?

75
05:26.880 --> 05:31.630
First, let us appreciate your cuteness.

76
05:31.630 --> 05:33.330
Guys!

77
05:33.330 --> 05:34.450
Worry not, Suzuki.

78
05:34.450 --> 05:38.390
We get it, you think Serizawa's cool.

79
05:40.520 --> 05:42.080
But the nose breathing...

80
05:42.080 --> 05:44.680
I know, right?

81
05:44.680 --> 05:47.130
This is no laughing matter!

82
05:47.130 --> 05:49.990
Saeki, let me practice with you.

83
05:49.990 --> 05:51.470
- Practice what? - Nose breathing.

84
05:51.470 --> 05:54.860
No way. Serizawa would kill me.

85
05:54.860 --> 05:55.990
Takeuchi, help me out.

86
05:55.990 --> 05:58.130
No thanks, I value my life.

87
05:58.130 --> 06:01.870
Iwasaki, you're nice. You'll help me, right?

88
06:01.870 --> 06:03.780
Sure, I don't mind.

89
06:03.780 --> 06:07.570
- Huh? - No!

90
06:07.570 --> 06:11.590
To summarize,

91
06:11.590 --> 06:15.260
you don't want to be the only one who's flustered?

92
06:15.260 --> 06:17.340
Yeah, I guess.

93
06:17.340 --> 06:22.510
Then just make Serizawa feel equally as flustered.

94
06:22.510 --> 06:25.350
Me, make Serizawa feel flustered?

95
06:25.350 --> 06:28.100
But how?

96
06:28.100 --> 06:32.010
Maybe you can use BL as a reference?

97
06:32.010 --> 06:33.660
- BL? - Yeah.

98
06:33.660 --> 06:35.610
That's a great idea.

99
06:35.610 --> 06:38.160
"Autumn, the time for BL".

100
06:38.160 --> 06:41.060
I call it, "Suzuki's Fall Fluster Strategy"!

101
06:41.060 --> 06:43.690
- Ta-da! - Ta-da.

102
06:43.690 --> 06:45.810
- I use BL as a reference... - Yeah.

103
06:45.810 --> 06:48.730
- To make Serizawa... - Yup.

104
06:51.150 --> 06:54.140
That's genius! Thanks guys!

105
06:54.140 --> 06:57.980
Fall Fluster Strategy.

106
06:57.980 --> 06:59.450
- Rolls off the tongue. - Yeah.

107
06:59.450 --> 07:01.020
Does it?

108
07:01.020 --> 07:04.180
Hey, he's taking notes.

109
07:04.180 --> 07:05.990
What's he gonna write?

110
07:07.040 --> 07:09.480
You're distracting me.

111
07:09.480 --> 07:10.560
Our bad.

112
07:10.560 --> 07:12.810
Maybe some background music will help?

113
07:12.810 --> 07:14.630
Yeah. Iwasaki, go.

114
07:14.630 --> 07:16.070
I can't think of a tune.

115
07:16.070 --> 07:18.990
- Just hum whatever. - You sure?

116
07:18.990 --> 07:21.350
- Maybe something classical. - Yeah.

117
07:40.650 --> 07:44.750
Do this... and then... after that...

118
07:48.710 --> 07:52.950
And finally...

119
07:52.950 --> 07:54.670
Okay.

120
07:54.670 --> 07:58.980
I will make Serizawa flustered today.

121
08:08.790 --> 08:10.100
Mission one.

122
08:10.100 --> 08:11.810
[Catch him off guard, and whisper in his ear]

123
08:12.790 --> 08:18.490
Whisper sweet nothings in his ear.

124
08:24.240 --> 08:25.880
Suzuki?

125
08:25.880 --> 08:27.570
Sorry!

126
08:28.480 --> 08:32.070
Did you just try to kiss my ear?

127
08:32.070 --> 08:33.870
No.

128
08:36.450 --> 08:39.180
So, that's what you like, huh?

129
08:39.180 --> 08:40.980
No!

130
08:43.200 --> 08:47.390
I'll give you one when we have time.

131
08:47.390 --> 08:49.600
You have it all wrong!

132
08:51.960 --> 08:54.820
Mission two.

133
08:54.820 --> 08:56.010
[The Wall Ambush]

134
08:56.010 --> 08:59.290
Cornering him against a wall. A surefire method.

135
08:59.290 --> 09:01.300
Later!

136
09:03.180 --> 09:05.720
For real? Tell me about it another time.

137
09:05.720 --> 09:08.740
- 'Sup, Serizawa. - Hey there.

138
09:10.940 --> 09:13.330
Okay, now!

139
09:17.810 --> 09:20.370
You okay?

140
09:20.370 --> 09:21.930
Yeah.

141
09:29.800 --> 09:32.330
Wanted some up-close time with me?

142
09:34.830 --> 09:36.500
Yup.

143
09:39.060 --> 09:43.300
Corndogs are made to be eaten with ketchup.

144
09:43.300 --> 09:45.870
Too bad I forgot the mustard.

145
09:52.440 --> 09:54.450
I'm not done yet.

146
09:54.450 --> 09:58.070
This time for sure... Mission three.

147
09:58.070 --> 10:00.260
Grab his arm,

148
10:00.260 --> 10:02.400
and forcefully snag a bite.

149
10:04.310 --> 10:06.160
Serizawa.

150
10:06.160 --> 10:08.980
Can I try a bite?

151
10:08.980 --> 10:10.810
Sure. Go ahead.

152
10:10.810 --> 10:12.750
Here.

153
10:12.750 --> 10:14.420
Now!

154
10:27.760 --> 10:29.970
You got ketchup all over.

155
10:29.970 --> 10:32.150
Really? Where?

156
10:38.030 --> 10:40.140
Thanks for the meal.

157
10:48.670 --> 10:50.550
This isn't working.

158
10:50.550 --> 10:53.050
[How to make Serizawa flustered]

159
10:53.050 --> 10:56.670
I can't make him flustered at all.

160
10:56.670 --> 11:01.160
If anything, I'm the one losing it!

161
11:03.580 --> 11:05.850
What's up?

162
11:07.400 --> 11:10.240
Look, Suzuki's got his head in his hands.

163
11:10.240 --> 11:12.970
Guess his plan was a failure?

164
11:12.970 --> 11:15.330
Maybe.

165
11:15.330 --> 11:18.630
Fine, fine.

166
11:19.590 --> 11:23.030
I'll go give him a hand.

167
11:23.030 --> 11:24.760
- A hand? - Yeah.

168
11:24.760 --> 11:26.290
Two, if he needs it.

169
11:26.290 --> 11:28.080
Both hands?

170
11:28.080 --> 11:31.140
- Yeah. - Whatever you say, boss.

171
11:34.720 --> 11:36.650
Wanna stop by the arcade?

172
11:36.650 --> 11:39.700
Sounds good to me.

173
11:39.700 --> 11:41.550
Come on.

174
11:41.550 --> 11:47.380
I guess I can't make him flustered after all.

175
11:49.540 --> 11:52.160
Suzuki. What's wrong?

176
11:52.160 --> 11:54.450
Everything.

177
11:54.450 --> 11:57.490
Serizawa doesn't get flustered at all.

178
11:57.490 --> 12:00.740
None of my plans worked.

179
12:02.740 --> 12:04.600
Let me see what you've got.

180
12:07.000 --> 12:10.450
Here, I'll let you in on a secret.

181
12:10.450 --> 12:12.880
- A secret? - Yeah.

182
12:12.880 --> 12:16.710
I'll tell you what makes Serizawa the most flustered.

183
12:16.710 --> 12:19.200
Dude, seriously?

184
12:19.200 --> 12:21.900
Come on, just for a day?

185
12:28.940 --> 12:30.190
- Really? - Yup.

186
12:30.190 --> 12:32.360
Hey, what're you two whispering about?

187
12:32.360 --> 12:35.060
See? Told you.

188
12:35.060 --> 12:37.660
What? What did he tell you?

189
12:38.980 --> 12:41.190
Saeki, what did you tell him?

190
12:41.190 --> 12:42.490
I'm not telling.

191
12:42.490 --> 12:44.980
It's my secret with Suzuki.

192
12:44.980 --> 12:46.910
What?

193
12:46.910 --> 12:48.260
Suzuki, come on.

194
12:48.260 --> 12:49.690
Huh?

195
12:52.460 --> 12:54.230
Let's go.

196
12:58.310 --> 13:01.080
Mission success.

197
13:06.200 --> 13:10.210
Suzuki. What was all that about?

198
13:10.210 --> 13:14.480
What were you two talking about? Tell me everything.

199
13:14.480 --> 13:16.690
Everything?

200
13:16.690 --> 13:19.610
Where should I start?

201
13:19.610 --> 13:22.500
From the beginning.

202
13:23.830 --> 13:25.870
Uh, okay.

203
13:25.870 --> 13:31.110
I started by asking the others for advice.

204
13:32.380 --> 13:39.090
Since you're way too cool and all.

205
13:42.360 --> 13:44.930
Not where I expected this to go.

206
13:44.930 --> 13:46.990
- Huh? - Never mind.

207
13:46.990 --> 13:48.990
And then?

208
13:48.990 --> 13:56.550
I wanted to practice nose breathing,

209
13:56.550 --> 13:59.950
so I tried asking the others for help.

210
13:59.950 --> 14:01.350
How studious.

211
14:01.350 --> 14:03.480
It's no laughing matter!

212
14:07.400 --> 14:11.570
That's another reason I like you.

213
14:11.570 --> 14:16.560
But seriously, never practice with them, okay?

214
14:16.560 --> 14:20.280
I'll always make time to help you.

215
14:20.280 --> 14:22.050
But...

216
14:22.050 --> 14:24.790
Your answer?

217
14:26.500 --> 14:28.190
Okay.

218
14:28.190 --> 14:32.130
And the only person you're allowed to kiss is?

219
14:32.130 --> 14:36.740
I only wanted to practice breathing through my nose, not...

220
14:36.740 --> 14:39.190
The only one you're allowed to kiss is?

221
14:40.490 --> 14:43.740
You.

222
14:43.740 --> 14:45.210
Good answer.

223
14:45.210 --> 14:47.670
So, what else did you ask about?

224
14:48.470 --> 14:54.300
I told them I didn't want to be the only one getting flustered.

225
14:54.300 --> 15:00.470
Their advice was to try and make you flustered, too.

226
15:03.060 --> 15:07.560
So, that's why you were acting weird today.

227
15:07.560 --> 15:11.280
That's when Saeki came up to me, and said...

228
15:12.110 --> 15:13.990
What?

229
15:13.990 --> 15:15.660
Tell me.

230
15:16.960 --> 15:23.520
Well, he said you lose your cool

231
15:25.070 --> 15:29.750
when you see me with others, and get jealous.

232
15:32.210 --> 15:34.520
Is that true?

233
15:37.710 --> 15:41.140
Don't go silent on me!

234
15:41.140 --> 15:42.810
Sorry.

235
15:42.810 --> 15:44.870
You just looked so cute

236
15:44.870 --> 15:50.710
struggling with the awkward silence.

237
15:51.830 --> 15:54.970
You have to stop it with that!

238
15:54.970 --> 15:56.690
S-Sorry!

239
15:58.500 --> 16:02.980
You pushed me down. Now that's a first.

240
16:04.410 --> 16:08.610
I'm so glad I lived to see this day.

241
16:08.610 --> 16:10.950
Dang it...

242
16:11.770 --> 16:15.010
I'm the only one who's flustered.

243
16:16.620 --> 16:20.350
How can you laugh while looking so composed?

244
16:20.350 --> 16:21.770
I feel beat.

245
16:21.770 --> 16:26.000
You're way too cool, dang it!

246
16:26.000 --> 16:29.040
Are you mad at me?

247
16:29.040 --> 16:30.270
Or are you complimenting me?

248
16:30.270 --> 16:33.780
Both! Geez...

249
16:38.330 --> 16:42.270
You're so adorable when you're mad.

250
16:42.270 --> 16:44.040
Quit teasing me.

251
16:44.040 --> 16:46.420
I'm not.

252
16:48.600 --> 16:50.750
Suzuki.

253
16:50.750 --> 16:54.730
It's all true, you know?

254
16:54.730 --> 16:56.360
Liar.

255
16:56.360 --> 16:58.060
I'm not lying.

256
16:58.060 --> 17:01.640
And I'm anything but composed.

257
17:01.640 --> 17:06.120
Did you know I've been holding back all day today?

258
17:06.120 --> 17:09.780
Your temptations almost swayed me.

259
17:11.840 --> 17:14.530
If you remember PE from the other day...

260
17:14.530 --> 17:15.690
I'm beat.

261
17:15.690 --> 17:18.680
- Points were docked. - For real?

262
17:18.680 --> 17:22.090
- Yikes. - I know right?

263
17:25.710 --> 17:27.710
Huh?

264
17:27.710 --> 17:31.710
You were so cute, I couldn't hold back,

265
17:31.710 --> 17:33.160
and dragged you into a bathroom stall.

266
17:33.160 --> 17:35.800
Serizawa!

267
17:35.800 --> 17:37.880
Wait, I can't breathe...

268
17:37.880 --> 17:41.020
Breathe in from your nose.

269
17:41.020 --> 17:43.710
You got this, Suzuki.

270
17:43.710 --> 17:45.970
What?

271
17:45.970 --> 17:48.390
That's a tall ask...

272
17:48.390 --> 17:50.060
That's why?

273
17:50.060 --> 17:52.720
Yeah. Sorry.

274
17:53.990 --> 17:58.700
Don't fan yourself like that in front of others ever again.

275
17:59.800 --> 18:03.050
And just the other day...

276
18:03.050 --> 18:07.020
Matsuno, I knew you'd like this new work

277
18:07.020 --> 18:09.170
- by Tatakiwari Ishibashi. - I see.

278
18:09.170 --> 18:10.770
- Wasn't the lead cool? - Yeah.

279
18:10.770 --> 18:14.700
Hasegawa's just the best.

280
18:14.700 --> 18:17.830
And Fukase's reaction is great, too!

281
18:17.830 --> 18:20.510
Suzuki. Come here.

282
18:20.510 --> 18:22.170
What's up?

283
18:33.160 --> 18:37.560
I saw you having fun with Matsuno,

284
18:37.560 --> 18:39.240
and couldn't help myself.

285
18:42.800 --> 18:45.260
That one I won't apologize for.

286
18:45.260 --> 18:48.190
Since it'll probably happen again.

287
18:48.190 --> 18:51.390
I had no idea.

288
18:51.390 --> 18:54.450
Yeah. I never told you.

289
18:54.450 --> 18:59.420
But that's how much I like you, Suzuki.

290
19:05.840 --> 19:10.840
Do you dislike tops who lose their cool

291
19:10.840 --> 19:14.110
and get jealous easily?

292
19:16.160 --> 19:18.900
No, of course not.

293
19:18.900 --> 19:20.900
If anything,

294
19:20.900 --> 19:25.340
I really like it that you do.

295
19:26.190 --> 19:32.870
Then, am I allowed to show my jealousy at school?

296
19:32.870 --> 19:36.120
Yeah. Go ahead.

297
19:36.120 --> 19:38.180
Really?

298
19:38.180 --> 19:41.840
My jealously can run deep though.

299
19:41.840 --> 19:43.360
Huh?

300
19:45.850 --> 19:48.350
Serizawa! Wait!

301
19:48.350 --> 19:49.830
No.

302
19:49.830 --> 19:53.470
I've been holding back all day.

303
19:53.470 --> 19:57.040
Now, it's time I counterattack.

304
20:02.380 --> 20:04.940
I love you, Suzuki.

305
20:05.690 --> 20:08.260
I won't ever let you go.

306
20:08.260 --> 20:10.280
Prepare yourself, okay?

307
20:37.470 --> 20:39.580
After that,

308
20:39.580 --> 20:45.370
I received Serizawa's onslaught of attacks for hours on end.

309
20:46.260 --> 20:48.230
Looks alike, right?

310
20:48.230 --> 20:49.780
Does not.

311
20:49.780 --> 20:50.990
It totally does!

312
20:50.990 --> 20:52.230
Morning.

313
20:52.230 --> 20:54.320
- Morning. - 'Sup?

314
20:54.320 --> 20:58.430
So, did you make up with Serizawa?

315
20:58.430 --> 21:01.540
Don't ask me about it.

316
21:01.540 --> 21:03.680
- Huh? - Okay?

317
21:05.070 --> 21:10.550
I never had a chance to doubt whether I was dreaming or not.

318
21:10.550 --> 21:12.230
It was really...

319
21:12.230 --> 21:15.300
Uh, what do we make of this?

320
21:15.300 --> 21:16.720
Suzuki.

321
21:16.720 --> 21:18.260
What did Serizawa do to you?

322
21:18.260 --> 21:20.520
- Hello? - What happened?

323
21:20.520 --> 21:22.890
- It was crazy. - What's up?

324
21:22.890 --> 21:25.880
Hey! You guys are too close.

325
21:25.880 --> 21:27.660
Huh?

326
21:29.290 --> 21:31.530
He's my Suzuki.

327
21:31.530 --> 21:34.450
Know your place.

328
21:34.450 --> 21:37.320
S-Serizawa?

329
21:37.320 --> 21:39.780
I told you, didn't I?

330
21:39.780 --> 21:44.720
I won't hold back on being jealous anymore.

331
21:44.720 --> 21:48.130
I mean, you did, but...

332
21:51.490 --> 21:54.720
Suzuki! You're way too close!

333
22:00.620 --> 22:01.620
Hey!

334
22:01.620 --> 22:03.660
That Serizawa...

335
22:03.660 --> 22:07.440
He really does act weird around Suzuki.

336
22:07.440 --> 22:09.950
You can say that again.

337
22:09.950 --> 22:12.530
What're they doing?

338
22:12.530 --> 22:14.900
Kabaddi?

339
22:14.900 --> 22:16.490
And there they go.

340
22:16.490 --> 22:18.710
- Maybe I'll join them. - No third wheeling.

341
22:18.710 --> 22:20.330
Me, too!

342
22:20.330 --> 22:22.730
Suzuki, wait up!

343
22:32.020 --> 22:34.210
Why did you run?

344
22:36.020 --> 22:40.130
Because you're being annoying.

345
22:40.130 --> 22:41.540
Really now.

346
22:41.540 --> 22:46.010
So, you don't like me?

347
22:46.760 --> 22:49.940
I do.

348
22:49.940 --> 22:51.690
I love you.
